ir3: keep the register banks inside the file without merged registers

{shared,std140}-array-struct-array-struct fault the a530 with status
C5C801C3 on every run and are skipped for it.  Their vertex shader uses 48
vec4 of full registers and 48 of half at once, and sweeping the two against
each other on a db820c puts the boundary at 512 half-units: the banks are
carved out of one file, and either may be used in full but not both.

Without merged registers ir3 sizes each bank on its own -- ctx->half.size is
RA_HALF_SIZE whatever ctx->full.size came to -- so the allocator may spend
384 + 192 half-units of a file that holds 512.  Cap the full bank at the file
minus what half needs, give the rest to half, and let the spiller aim at the
same budget.

Both ends of the bound follow the hardware's whole-vec4 granularity: the
full budget rounds down so its own footprint stays inside it, and the half
reservation rounds up because a bank holding a single component still costs
a whole register.  A bound landing mid-register would otherwise leave the
allocation one over.  Half is only reserved when the shader uses any.

Forcing !mergedregs on an a650 reproduces the same fault, so key on that
rather than on the generation.

Closes: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/issues/7159
